      "Refer all sickle cell patients with bleeding into the eye, priapism, haematuria or renal disease and stroke to a specialist. The presence of osteomyelitis, aseptic necrosis of the hip, acute chest syndrome and persistent jaundice after initial management as recommended above should also warrant a referral to a specialist centre. Patients with CNS events, unexplained high white cell and platelet counts (more than 15 and 500 x 109/L respectively), intractable morbid pain, repetitive crises or recurrent severe anaemia interfering with their lives should be referred to a specialist."
