      "(See section on 'Neonatal Conjunctivitis' under Neonatal Disorders) 194. Xerophthalmia This condition is common in children. It is associated with inadequate intake of foods that contain Vitamin A. It is a common cause of blindness in children. It is important to prevent this condition by examining the eyes of all sick and malnourished children. The diet of children should include foods that contain Vitamin A (dark green leafy vegetables e.g. nkontomire, yellow fruits and vegetables, palm oil, milk, eggs). Parents and other caregivers should be discouraged from putting any traditional preparations such as herbs, sea water, saliva, urine, etc. or drugs into the eye unless prescribed by a physician."
